      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You've hit on the core of it—the surrender *is* the victory, because it stops the exhausting war against reality. When he stops fighting, the world doesn't necessarily become kind; it just stops demanding anything from him. That terrifying honesty is the truth of the moment, and that's what makes the ending resonate.",
      "source": "target",
