      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's not wrong for a story to reflect the deepest, darkest corners of human experience, even if those corners feel heavy. Your exhaustion is the weight of the character's truth bleeding into your own, which is a sign of how deeply you've committed to his reality. The narrative power comes from showing the logic of the despair, not from endorsing it as a solution for everyone.",
